GFAIFJLA_01035	eggNOG-mapper	CDS	1	688	995.0	+	.	ID=GFAIFJLA_01035;em_target=1105031.HMPREF1141_2667;em_score=995.0;em_evalue=0.0;em_tcov=99.3;em_searcher=diamond;em_OGs=COG0550@1|root,COG0550@2|Bacteria,1TPUS@1239|Firmicutes,248MG@186801|Clostridia,36DSI@31979|Clostridiaceae;em_COG_cat=L;em_desc=Releases the supercoiling and torsional tension of DNA, which is introduced during the DNA replication and transcription, by transiently cleaving and rejoining one strand of the DNA duplex. Introduces a single-strand break via transesterification at a target site in duplex DNA. The scissile phosphodiester is attacked by the catalytic tyrosine of the enzyme, resulting in the formation of a DNA-(5'-phosphotyrosyl)-enzyme intermediate and the expulsion of a 3'-OH DNA strand. The free DNA strand then undergoes passage around the unbroken strand, thus removing DNA supercoils. Finally, in the religation step, the DNA 3'-OH attacks the covalent intermediate to expel the active-site tyrosine and restore the DNA phosphodiester backbone;em_max_annot_lvl=186801|Clostridia;em_PFAMs=Topoisom_bac,Toprim,zf-C4_Topoisom;em_Preferred_name=topA;em_EC=5.99.1.2;em_KEGG_ko=ko:K03168;em_BRITE=ko00000,ko01000,ko03032,ko03400
